  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are participating in an elite chess tournament for 444 people in the world only.\n\nThere are prizes in this tournament, obviously. If you finish rank iii, you get 1000⋅24−i1000 \\cdot 2^{4 - i}1000⋅24−i rupees. Thus, the prizes are as follows:\n\n\nRank 111: 800080008000 rupees\nRank 222: 400040004000 rupees\nRank 333: 200020002000 rupees\nRank 444: 100010001000 rupees\nYou finished at rank XXX. How much prize money did you win?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input contains a single integer XXX, your rank.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput the amount of prize money you won in rupees.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤X≤41 \\le X \\le 41≤X≤4"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1",
        "output": "8000",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nAs explained in the statement, rank 111 wins 1000⋅2(4−1)=80001000 \\cdot 2^{(4 - 1)} = 80001000⋅2(4−1)=8000 rupees."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4",
        "output": "1000",
        "explanation": ""
      }
    ]
  },
